  ============================================================================
  RM_TheChillFloorLife.xml            TerminalBiomes · authored 2026-09-26
  ============================================================================
  SEA_FISHABLES_ALIVE_IN_DEPTHS_1 — the CHILL portion.

  Owner, at the bench 2026-09-26, typed:
      "All the fishables should also be alive and moving around in the depths
       (this is true for ALL seas)."

  ⇒ A catch item with nothing swimming is HALF a species. The Chill's
  own PROPANELAKE_ANIMALDENSITY_ZERO_1 blocker (animalDensity left at 0f) is
  now CLOSED — RM_TheChill.xml sets animalDensity 0.08 — so this pass is
  no longer authoring dead content.

  Of the Chill's nine fishTypes rows, RM_HeeminCatch/RM_OovanamCatch
  already pair with RM_Heemin/RM_Oovanam (RM_TheChillFauna.xml), and
  RUT_Zhiil already pairs with RM_Vaunoom — the catch item's own comment
  says outright: "the young of the V-wake exotic — the catch is the young,
  the owed V-wake adult PawnKindDef is the floor pairing, per the owner's
  life-stage carve-out" — that IS a living counterpart (a life-stage pair),
  already built, nothing to add. The remaining SIX catch-only rows
  (RUT_Fessu, RUT_Krellik, RUT_Oddu, RUT_Oovu, RUT_Iliss, RUT_Tarnn) get
  bodies here.

  ============================================================================
  🔑 AUTHORED FROM THE CATCH ITEMS' OWN DESCRIPTIONS, NOT INVENTED
  ============================================================================
  src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/RUT_PropaneLakeCatch_Items.xml
  already describes every one of these six in full: a paper-thin crystal
  fish that "feeds by growing," a frost-plated crab that molts nightly, a
  sessile jelly-sac shellfish kin to the shore's rime nodule, a harmless
  floating frost-bell, a conductive wire-thin eel that feeds on ground
  current, and an ambiguous branching crystal colony "half frozen
  hydrocarbon and half something alive." Every body size, speed, diet and
  behaviour flag below is read off those sentences. ⛔ Nothing here was made
  up; if a number looks odd, check the item text before "fixing" it.

  ============================================================================
  🔴 TIER: THESE ARE RM_, THE CATCH ITEMS ARE RUT_ — same shape as the Grey
  ============================================================================
  All six catch items ship as RUT_Fessu etc. in the Utinni patch layer,
  MayRequire-gated on mandrake.rut.patches. Every name is an INVENTED exotic
  word, not canon IP, so Q11a (biome_mod_architecture.md §7) routes the
  living counterparts to RM_ and inline on RM_TheChill with no
  MayRequire — the free mod's floor has to stand alone. The CATCH side is
  the half still in the wrong tier, same as RM_GreySeaFloorLife.xml's own
  header records for the Grey — OWED, not this wave's to fix.

  ============================================================================
  NO WILD PLANTS ON THIS BIOME — every species is OmnivoreAnimal
  ============================================================================
  RM_TheChill carries no <wildPlants> and no <plantDensity> at all (it
  defaults to 0f — the same silent-kill trap CLAUDE.md documents for other
  biomes). A VegetarianAnimal here would starve outright. Every race below
  is OmnivoreAnimal, matching RM_Heemin/RM_Oovanam/RM_Hoolen's own choice.

  ============================================================================
  THE HARD BANS (the_propane_lakes.md §6), checked one by one
  ============================================================================
  Ban 1 (no icy dayside analogs): every species below is invented fresh from
        its own catch description, not a reskinned dayside animal.
  Ban 2 (no kyber): RM_Tarnn is a branching crystal colony and is written,
        like its catch item, to explicitly NOT be kyber or lightsaber-
        adjacent — no such property on this def, ever.
  Ban 3 (no visibility penalty as the standing state): none of these six
        emit fog, darkness or an aim penalty.
  Ban 4 (no ignition without a hot source or spark): none of these six
        ignites anything; Flammability is an ITEM-side stat (the catch
        defs), not carried onto the living race.
  Ban 6 (no transportable natives, R-H10): trainability None throughout,
        same as every other Chill resident.

  PLACEHOLDER ART: flat silhouette PNGs at Things/Pawn/Animal/<defName>/,
  256x256 RGBA, Graphic_Single — same posture the Propane's existing three
  residents already use. Checked infrastructure/artpipe/done/ and _artsrc/
  first (MEASURED 2026-09-26): no existing render for fessu/krellik/oddu/
  oovu/iliss/tarnn under any spelling. Real art queued to artpipe this pass.
  ============================================================================
-->
