    <!-- CHILL_GARDEN_DEFENSE_1, 2026-09-28 — "things catalogued as scenery
         stand up and fight." Every RM_Tarnn that will ever exist is spawned
         exclusively by GenStep_SeaFloorFauna reading THIS biome's
         <wildAnimals> (MEASURED off that GenStep's own header: a sea
         BiomeDef's wildAnimals is never consulted by vanilla's ambient
         spawner, so that GenStep — which runs only when generating the
         Chill's seabed pocket map — is the only place a Tarnn is ever
         created), so starting dormant here can never strand a hypothetical
         surface-spawned Tarnn. jobDormancy=true (not signal-driven — the
         wake is always an explicit RM_MapComponent_ChillGardenDefense call,
         WakeUp() + a forced ManhunterPermanent, never a passive proximity
         trigger) shows the sleeping Zzz and keeps a dormant Tarnn from
         acting, exactly the "ancient danger room" scenery-until-disturbed
         read the ruling asks for. RM_CompTarnnRoused is what actually makes
         a woken Tarnn a threat — see that file's header for the full
